    "notes": "SUMMARY:\nMON price $0.0242 (-0.23% 24h per snapshot; broader decline from $0.034 Oct 1 to $0.029 Oct 6, now recovering slightly). Monad TVL down 3.3% over 7d to $1.007B. Realized volatility high: 82.78% 24h, 415% 7d (thin history: 36 returns vs 150 needed). Oracle-pool deviation 2.27 bps, pool tight. Market reports show profit-taking after 30%+ late-Sept rally.\n\nCHANGES:\n1. MON_UNLOCK_CLIFF (Nov 24): 16.61B MON (~16.6% of supply) vests across Team (10.7B), Investors (5.3B), Category Labs (1.07B). Estimated value $408-520M (exceeds current circulating supply ~11.8B). Investors entered at $0.0115/MON vs. current $0.024. Web reports dominant on unlock sell-pressure risk.\n\n2. TVL_CONTRACTION: Down 3.3% over 7d from record highs (Q3 peaked Oct 1 at $1.042B, now $1.007B on Oct 9). Snapshot shows 30-day history: gradual decline from Sept 10-16, recovery to Oct 1, then declining Oct 7-9. Broader activity metrics stable (Uniswap V4 leading DEX volume).\n\n3. VOLATILITY_SPIKE: 7d annualized vol 415% (THIN_HISTORY warning—only 36 returns). 24h vol 82.78%. Market reports describe recent action as profit-taking correction, not fundamental breakdown. $0.027 identified as key support (breakout level Sept 30); below that, pre-breakout range $0.025-0.026.\n\n4. ECOSYSTEM_GROWTH_OFFSET: Web sources highlight Q3 growth (3x TVL expansion, record daily transactions/DEX volume). Announced catalysts: privacy upgrade (Oct 6 event), stablecoin expansion (StraitsX XSGD/XUSD early 2027). However, analyst c"
